WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Nitrate is reduced to nitrite by nitrate reductase, then to ammonium by nitrite reductase.

00:07.000 --> 00:15.000
Ammonium nitrogen can enter amino acids.

00:15.000 --> 00:22.000
This is a pathway outline; it omits reductant, protons, water and full reaction stoichiometry.

00:22.000 --> 00:29.000
External nutrient supply is maintained.

00:29.000 --> 00:35.000
The reference tissue experiences twelve hours of light, then twelve of darkness, repeated twice.

00:35.000 --> 00:42.000
The light regime changes the prescribed uptake and assimilation capacities.

00:42.000 --> 00:52.000
Uptake and assimilation continue at lower rates in the dark in this example.

00:52.000 --> 01:02.000
Internal nitrogen reserves change because the two rates differ.

01:02.000 --> 01:12.000
Stored carbon and energy are assumed sufficient; neither growth nor carbon exhaustion is modelled.

01:12.000 --> 01:24.000
An illustrative processing response rises to a maximum and declines at high irradiance.

01:24.000 --> 01:36.000
The peak is chosen for teaching, not measured for a species.

01:36.000 --> 01:48.000
Increasing light can help in one range and harm in another.

01:48.000 --> 01:57.000
The example peaks at twenty degrees Celsius.

01:57.000 --> 02:07.000
A Q10 value describes a rate ratio over a stated temperature interval.

02:07.000 --> 02:16.000
It does not justify indefinite doubling or identify an optimum from two temperatures.

02:16.000 --> 02:29.000
In Smit 2002, Gracilaria gracilis showed approximately thirty-eight percent suppression of nitrate uptake with ammonium above five micromoles per litre.

02:29.000 --> 02:42.000
The bars are a normalised summary, not raw paired measurements or a fitted inhibition function.

02:42.000 --> 02:49.000
The total curve here is the sum of two saturating components with different concentration scales.

02:49.000 --> 02:57.000
Its additional rise is an illustrative biphasic response.

02:57.000 --> 03:04.000
Curve shape alone does not establish transporter identity, a switch to passive transport or energetic cost.

03:04.000 --> 03:12.000
Measure local nutrient concentration and uptake per unit tissue or active surface under matched conditions.

03:12.000 --> 03:20.000
Cross a light or temperature treatment with water movement, include replicates and state what outcomes distinguish the proposed mechanisms.
